{
  "$comment": [
    "The Console EQ family's parameters, declared once.",
    "",
    "Both the C++ setter dispatch and the TypeScript control table are GENERATED",
    "from this file by scripts/generate-params.mjs. Neither is hand-written and",
    "neither may be hand-edited — that is what makes Ledger cell D1's first half",
    "unconstructible rather than tested.",
    "",
    "TWO LINEAGES, ONE DEVICE, AND BOTH SETS OF CONTROLS ARE HERE. dyn-05 covers",
    "both because Motion Wave builds one console-EQ family and the two differ in",
    "ways that matter to the DSP rather than to the presets: one has real",
    "inductors and a high-pass filter, the other has bridged-T networks and a",
    "band-pass, and §10 test 19 asserts they do not share a filter engine. The",
    "lineage switch selects which set is in circuit; the other set's controls",
    "still exist, because a user switching back must find their settings where",
    "they left them.",
    "",
    "The amounts are stepped on the American side and continuous on the British.",
    "That is §8's table and not an oversight: the American panel is a detented",
    "switch with five positions each way, and its step values (2, 4, 6, 9, 12)",
    "are not a series — the gap widens at the top — so the control selects from a",
    "table rather than scaling a range."
  ],
  "unit": "dyn-05",
  "className": "ConsoleEq",
  "header": "../console_eq.h",
  "namespace": "mw::units",
  "tsPrefix": "console_eq",
  "tsTarget": "motionwave/ui/units/console_eq/params.gen.ts",
  "params": [
